The Thunderbolt port selects GPL-2.0 (GPL-2.0-only for the DP-IN files).
No firmware, host DROM, device identity, calibration or hardware capture is included.

upstream/apple-dpin-* files are byte-for-byte source copies of
Omacom linux-aurora 6a08a08e, drivers/thunderbolt/ (SHA256 in provenance.json).
They retain their SPDX notices. The parent Apple ACIO/NHI driver is:
  Copyright (c) Sven Peter <sven@kernel.org>

src/pd_apple_nhi.c and include/pd_apple_nhi.h adapt Apple register layout,
ring configuration, SRAM checks and T8103 DP-IN from apple.c, and the ring
start/stop/descriptor sequence from nhi.c/nhi_regs.h/include/linux/thunderbolt.h:
  Copyright (c) Sven Peter <sven@kernel.org>
  Copyright (c) 2014 Andreas Noever <andreas.noever@gmail.com>
  Copyright (C) 2018 Intel Corporation

src/pd_cio_lifecycle.c adapts apple_cio_start/stop ordering from apple.c,
Copyright (c) Sven Peter. src/pd_dpin_policy.c copies its platform policy.
The NHI policy constants and test-only topology predicate retain the Linux
GPL-2.0 notice and the nhi.h/tb.h copyright attribution above.

New portability type/errno/bit headers and host assertion/OF fixtures are MIT;
they implement no hardware or connection manager. The OF, KUnit and topology
fixtures are only used by host tests, not by the SDK object target.

upstream/family/ and pininc/ are unmodified Omacom linux-aurora sources
at the full revision and per-file SHA256 in family-provenance.json. They
retain all original SPDX/copyright notices. These are the connection-manager,
control-channel, topology, path and tunnel implementations; no native
Thunderbolt attachment is implied by their inclusion.

src/pd_cio_tunables.c and include/pd_cio_tunables.h adapt the raw 24-byte
ACIO format and eleven T8103 group mappings from m1n1 src/kboot.c at
121fcbf35d4501814b58ca5347926a4173b6a512 (MIT), and register clear/OR-set
semantics from Linux drivers/soc/apple/tunable.c (GPL-2.0-only OR MIT).
